[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186162134 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b5d80cd0-76ca-5260-b15c-cf7c6e9faf1e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b5d80cd0-76ca-5260-b15c-cf7c6e9faf1e" :question/id #uuid "b5d80cd0-76ca-5260-b15c-cf7c6e9faf1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-146309" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16}xy,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 4, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the covariance between $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The joint support of $X$ and $Y$ is given by the rectangle \n\n$$\nS=[0,2]\\times [0,4].\n$$\n\nMoreover, we can write \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=g(x)\\cdot h(y),\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $h(y)=\\frac{y}{8}.$ \n\nTherefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent, and consequently $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fc18d19d-57df-5431-9db5-d3ea0a3393eb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fc18d19d-57df-5431-9db5-d3ea0a3393eb" "answer-ec09683f-97e8-5921-86c5-63360bce02d8" "answer-b4aaf98a-33ad-537d-a3f0-b7504ddda61e" "answer-5a8298a5-fac1-5365-b909-1315a53989cc" "answer-b3de5092-4946-5d3e-b8a7-ad0de03a3d23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc18d19d-57df-5431-9db5-d3ea0a3393eb" :answer/id #uuid "fc18d19d-57df-5431-9db5-d3ea0a3393eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec09683f-97e8-5921-86c5-63360bce02d8" :answer/id #uuid "ec09683f-97e8-5921-86c5-63360bce02d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4aaf98a-33ad-537d-a3f0-b7504ddda61e" :answer/id #uuid "b4aaf98a-33ad-537d-a3f0-b7504ddda61e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a8298a5-fac1-5365-b909-1315a53989cc" :answer/id #uuid "5a8298a5-fac1-5365-b909-1315a53989cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3de5092-4946-5d3e-b8a7-ad0de03a3d23" :answer/id #uuid "b3de5092-4946-5d3e-b8a7-ad0de03a3d23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162136 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-aa0cadd2-5104-5faa-b07c-30440395ac28" "question-7980335d-9e66-542b-a520-d910d32ed247"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-aa0cadd2-5104-5faa-b07c-30440395ac28" :question/id #uuid "aa0cadd2-5104-5faa-b07c-30440395ac28" :question/math-academy-id "q-146386" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n\nIf $\\text{E}[X]=0.8$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=2.2,$ calculate the covariance between $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nWe use the rule of the lazy statistician to find $\\text{E}[XY]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =(0)(1)(0.1)+(0)(2)(0.2)+(0)(3)(0.3) \\\\  & +(2)(1)(0.1)+(2)(2)(0.2)+(2)(3)(0.1) \\\\  & =1.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =1.6-(0.8)(2.2) \\\\  & =-0.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7d5afdc4-e07a-5a57-8ed5-dcac00f594d4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a2068b7-fdfd-5f88-ba30-9e61e314cded" "answer-f7f016d4-5401-5ddf-a3fa-995c56e2b641" "answer-7d5afdc4-e07a-5a57-8ed5-dcac00f594d4" "answer-e68e66b9-7d4c-558f-ba74-7cf21592d21e" "answer-0e328848-6235-5d28-83bb-5262dbf27fb7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a2068b7-fdfd-5f88-ba30-9e61e314cded" :answer/id #uuid "2a2068b7-fdfd-5f88-ba30-9e61e314cded" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.05" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7f016d4-5401-5ddf-a3fa-995c56e2b641" :answer/id #uuid "f7f016d4-5401-5ddf-a3fa-995c56e2b641" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d5afdc4-e07a-5a57-8ed5-dcac00f594d4" :answer/id #uuid "7d5afdc4-e07a-5a57-8ed5-dcac00f594d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e68e66b9-7d4c-558f-ba74-7cf21592d21e" :answer/id #uuid "e68e66b9-7d4c-558f-ba74-7cf21592d21e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.04" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e328848-6235-5d28-83bb-5262dbf27fb7" :answer/id #uuid "0e328848-6235-5d28-83bb-5262dbf27fb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.08" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162132 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e6e3c2bf-143f-5ac7-a0ed-5faf8562286b" "question-29a09d79-668a-5d76-93b7-d90b94b6b6a1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e6e3c2bf-143f-5ac7-a0ed-5faf8562286b" :question/id #uuid "e6e3c2bf-143f-5ac7-a0ed-5faf8562286b" :question/math-academy-id "q-147965" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.11$ | $0.44$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.09$ | $0.36$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$\n\n*Hint: It can be shown that $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible values of $x$ and $y.$*" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nWe're told that\n\n$$\nP(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)\n$$\n\nfor all possible values of $x$ and $y.$ Therefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent. \n\nSince $X$ are $Y$ are independent, we have $\\text{Cov}(X,Y)=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a285d13c-8e91-53ff-befc-22c00f6c4f72"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a285d13c-8e91-53ff-befc-22c00f6c4f72" :answer-field/id #uuid "a285d13c-8e91-53ff-befc-22c00f6c4f72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9f890194-e25d-57ba-b7d6-5ea090499c5b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f890194-e25d-57ba-b7d6-5ea090499c5b" "answer-3a0eed03-c823-52d2-9d91-5f4f57fccf4b" "answer-c6be9011-10e2-579c-9b58-794b4bedb4ae" "answer-007b88eb-e604-58da-b447-a95dc8bd2d6a" "answer-75de5ea3-85e7-5be2-9550-6f79d2d4cd24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f890194-e25d-57ba-b7d6-5ea090499c5b" :answer/id #uuid "9f890194-e25d-57ba-b7d6-5ea090499c5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a0eed03-c823-52d2-9d91-5f4f57fccf4b" :answer/id #uuid "3a0eed03-c823-52d2-9d91-5f4f57fccf4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.01" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6be9011-10e2-579c-9b58-794b4bedb4ae" :answer/id #uuid "c6be9011-10e2-579c-9b58-794b4bedb4ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.03" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-007b88eb-e604-58da-b447-a95dc8bd2d6a" :answer/id #uuid "007b88eb-e604-58da-b447-a95dc8bd2d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75de5ea3-85e7-5be2-9550-6f79d2d4cd24" :answer/id #uuid "75de5ea3-85e7-5be2-9550-6f79d2d4cd24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-29a09d79-668a-5d76-93b7-d90b94b6b6a1" :question/id #uuid "29a09d79-668a-5d76-93b7-d90b94b6b6a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-147969" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.6$ | $0$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.6$ | $0$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.85$ | $0.15$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.4+2\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0+1.2 \\\\  & =1.2 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.85+1\\cdot 0.15 \\\\  & =0+0.15 \\\\  & =0.15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-1.2)(y-0.15)f(x,y) \\\\  & =(0-1.2)(0-0.15)f(0,0) \\\\  & +(0-1.2)(1-0.15)f(0,1) \\\\  & +(2-1.2)(0-0.15)f(2,0) \\\\  & +(2-1.2)(1-0.15)f(2,1) \\\\  & =(-1.2)(-0.15)(0.25) \\\\  & +(-1.2)(0.85)(0.15) \\\\  & +(0.8)(-0.15)(0.6) \\\\  & +(0.8)(0.85)(0) \\\\  & =-0.18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3ffdfa5d-c95f-54fd-857a-e11023b0bfbe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3ffdfa5d-c95f-54fd-857a-e11023b0bfbe" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ffdfa5d-c95f-54fd-857a-e11023b0bfbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4995e421-f57e-506e-949a-56fe54b64747" :answer-field/choices ["answer-63fbbf28-a5eb-5784-8ae2-bdb3e9bd5c6c" "answer-3ed2e7fa-1b4e-554a-9f21-5c4c18fb3212" "answer-4995e421-f57e-506e-949a-56fe54b64747" "answer-372acec4-20fe-5117-a2b8-fe4b93514f94" "answer-36fcb00a-f41b-5217-896a-1c21c8eca096"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63fbbf28-a5eb-5784-8ae2-bdb3e9bd5c6c" :answer/id #uuid "63fbbf28-a5eb-5784-8ae2-bdb3e9bd5c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.06" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ed2e7fa-1b4e-554a-9f21-5c4c18fb3212" :answer/id #uuid "3ed2e7fa-1b4e-554a-9f21-5c4c18fb3212" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.09" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4995e421-f57e-506e-949a-56fe54b64747" :answer/id #uuid "4995e421-f57e-506e-949a-56fe54b64747" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-372acec4-20fe-5117-a2b8-fe4b93514f94" :answer/id #uuid "372acec4-20fe-5117-a2b8-fe4b93514f94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36fcb00a-f41b-5217-896a-1c21c8eca096" :answer/id #uuid "36fcb00a-f41b-5217-896a-1c21c8eca096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7980335d-9e66-542b-a520-d910d32ed247" :question/id #uuid "7980335d-9e66-542b-a520-d910d32ed247" :question/math-academy-id "q-148013" :question/problem "If $\\text{E}[X]=5.5,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=4.38,$ and $\\text{E}[XY]=24.12$ for two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =24.12-(5.5)\\cdot (4.38) \\\\  & =0.03.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of $X$ and $Y$ is $0.03.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c0679843-7790-5fe7-98d3-601893fb4657"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c0679843-7790-5fe7-98d3-601893fb4657" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0679843-7790-5fe7-98d3-601893fb4657" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c46f447f-df24-5902-9689-fea13287bce2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c46f447f-df24-5902-9689-fea13287bce2" "answer-b9b31986-b655-51df-be39-4f4da4a378d8" "answer-5534a32e-c646-5abb-8671-2e12e1a26b9a" "answer-763c6049-7824-5f86-a7d7-d2da13ebd71a" "answer-bd241af9-776b-59c5-81bc-13df08d53c71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c46f447f-df24-5902-9689-fea13287bce2" :answer/id #uuid "c46f447f-df24-5902-9689-fea13287bce2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.03" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9b31986-b655-51df-be39-4f4da4a378d8" :answer/id #uuid "b9b31986-b655-51df-be39-4f4da4a378d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.07" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5534a32e-c646-5abb-8671-2e12e1a26b9a" :answer/id #uuid "5534a32e-c646-5abb-8671-2e12e1a26b9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-763c6049-7824-5f86-a7d7-d2da13ebd71a" :answer/id 