id "4f7e1c6e-7d68-545c-b26a-04a011d3cdbd" :step/content "question-7980335d-9e66-542b-a520-d910d32ed247" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-b5d80cd0-76ca-5260-b15c-cf7c6e9faf1e" :question/id #uuid "b5d80cd0-76ca-5260-b15c-cf7c6e9faf1e"] ["question-b5d80cd0-76ca-5260-b15c-cf7c6e9faf1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-146309"] ["question-b5d80cd0-76ca-5260-b15c-cf7c6e9faf1e" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16}xy,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 4, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the covariance between $X$ and $Y.$"] ["question-b5d80cd0-76ca-5260-b15c-cf7c6e9faf1e" :question/worked-solution "The joint support of $X$ and $Y$ is given by the rectangle \n\n$$\nS=[0,2]\\times [0,4].\n$$\n\nMoreover, we can write \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=g(x)\\cdot h(y),\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $h(y)=\\frac{y}{8}.$ \n\nTherefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent, and consequently $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.$"] ["question-b5d80cd0-76ca-5260-b15c-cf7c6e9faf1e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc"] ["answer-fc18d19d-57df-5431-9db5-d3ea0a3393eb" :answer/id #uuid "fc18d19d-57df-5431-9db5-d3ea0a3393eb"] ["answer-fc18d19d-57df-5431-9db5-d3ea0a3393eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fc18d19d-57df-5431-9db5-d3ea0a3393eb" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-ec09683f-97e8-5921-86c5-63360bce02d8" :answer/id #uuid "ec09683f-97e8-5921-86c5-63360bce02d8"] ["answer-ec09683f-97e8-5921-86c5-63360bce02d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ec09683f-97e8-5921-86c5-63360bce02d8" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-b4aaf98a-33ad-537d-a3f0-b7504ddda61e" :answer/id #uuid "b4aaf98a-33ad-537d-a3f0-b7504ddda61e"] ["answer-b4aaf98a-33ad-537d-a3f0-b7504ddda61e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b4aaf98a-33ad-537d-a3f0-b7504ddda61e" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-5a8298a5-fac1-5365-b909-1315a53989cc" :answer/id #uuid "5a8298a5-fac1-5365-b909-1315a53989cc"] ["answer-5a8298a5-fac1-5365-b909-1315a53989cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5a8298a5-fac1-5365-b909-1315a53989cc" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["answer-b3de5092-4946-5d3e-b8a7-ad0de03a3d23" :answer/id #uuid "b3de5092-4946-5d3e-b8a7-ad0de03a3d23"] ["answer-b3de5092-4946-5d3e-b8a7-ad0de03a3d23" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b3de5092-4946-5d3e-b8a7-ad0de03a3d23" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["answer-field-5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc" :answer-field/correct "answer-fc18d19d-57df-5431-9db5-d3ea0a3393eb"] ["answer-field-5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc" :answer-field/choices "answer-fc18d19d-57df-5431-9db5-d3ea0a3393eb"] ["answer-field-5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc" :answer-field/choices "answer-ec09683f-97e8-5921-86c5-63360bce02d8"] ["answer-field-5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc" :answer-field/choices "answer-b4aaf98a-33ad-537d-a3f0-b7504ddda61e"] ["answer-field-5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc" :answer-field/choices "answer-5a8298a5-fac1-5365-b909-1315a53989cc"] ["answer-field-5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc" :answer-field/choices "answer-b3de5092-4946-5d3e-b8a7-ad0de03a3d23"] ["question-b5d80cd0-76ca-5260-b15c-cf7c6e9faf1e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-5e342586-6b50-54ec-9bac-5940a5f9cadc"] [17592186162134 :knowledge-point/questions "question-b5d80cd0-76ca-5260-b15c-cf7c6e9faf1e"] ["question-aa0cadd2-5104-5faa-b07c-30440395ac28" :question/id #uuid "aa0cadd2-5104-5faa-b07c-30440395ac28"] ["question-aa0cadd2-5104-5faa-b07c-30440395ac28" :question/math-academy-id "q-146386"] ["question-aa0cadd2-5104-5faa-b07c-30440395ac28" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n\nIf $\\text{E}[X]=0.8$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=2.2,$ calculate the covariance between $X$ and $Y.$"] ["question-aa0cadd2-5104-5faa-b07c-30440395ac28" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nWe use the rule of the lazy statistician to find $\\text{E}[XY]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =(0)(1)(0.1)+(0)(2)(0.2)+(0)(3)(0.3) \\\\  & +(2)(1)(0.1)+(2)(2)(0.2)+(2)(3)(0.1) \\\\  & =1.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =1.6-(0.8)(2.2) \\\\  & =-0.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-aa0cadd2-5104-5faa-b07c-30440395ac28" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e"] ["answer-2a2068b7-fdfd-5f88-ba30-9e61e314cded" :answer/id #uuid "2a2068b7-fdfd-5f88-ba30-9e61e314cded"] ["answer-2a2068b7-fdfd-5f88-ba30-9e61e314cded" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2a2068b7-fdfd-5f88-ba30-9e61e314cded" :answer/value "-0.05"] ["answer-f7f016d4-5401-5ddf-a3fa-995c56e2b641" :answer/id #uuid "f7f016d4-5401-5ddf-a3fa-995c56e2b641"] ["answer-f7f016d4-5401-5ddf-a3fa-995c56e2b641" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f7f016d4-5401-5ddf-a3fa-995c56e2b641" :answer/value "-0.12"] ["answer-7d5afdc4-e07a-5a57-8ed5-dcac00f594d4" :answer/id #uuid "7d5afdc4-e07a-5a57-8ed5-dcac00f594d4"] ["answer-7d5afdc4-e07a-5a57-8ed5-dcac00f594d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7d5afdc4-e07a-5a57-8ed5-dcac00f594d4" :answer/value "-0.16"] ["answer-e68e66b9-7d4c-558f-ba74-7cf21592d21e" :answer/id #uuid "e68e66b9-7d4c-558f-ba74-7cf21592d21e"] ["answer-e68e66b9-7d4c-558f-ba74-7cf21592d21e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e68e66b9-7d4c-558f-ba74-7cf21592d21e" :answer/value "0.04"] ["answer-0e328848-6235-5d28-83bb-5262dbf27fb7" :answer/id #uuid "0e328848-6235-5d28-83bb-5262dbf27fb7"] ["answer-0e328848-6235-5d28-83bb-5262dbf27fb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0e328848-6235-5d28-83bb-5262dbf27fb7" :answer/value "0.08"] ["answer-field-1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e" :answer-field/correct "answer-7d5afdc4-e07a-5a57-8ed5-dcac00f594d4"] ["answer-field-1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e" :answer-field/choices "answer-2a2068b7-fdfd-5f88-ba30-9e61e314cded"] ["answer-field-1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e" :answer-field/choices "answer-f7f016d4-5401-5ddf-a3fa-995c56e2b641"] ["answer-field-1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e" :answer-field/choices "answer-7d5afdc4-e07a-5a57-8ed5-dcac00f594d4"] ["answer-field-1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e" :answer-field/choices "answer-e68e66b9-7d4c-558f-ba74-7cf21592d21e"] ["answer-field-1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e" :answer-field/choices "answer-0e328848-6235-5d28-83bb-5262dbf27fb7"] ["question-aa0cadd2-5104-5faa-b07c-30440395ac28" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-1c0dff92-4fab-57ce-b774-785d56a0ed4e"] [17592186162136 :knowledge-point/questions "question-aa0cadd2-5104-5faa-b07c-30440395ac28"] ["question-e6e3c2bf-143f-5ac7-a0ed-5faf8562286b" :question/id #uuid "e6e3c2bf-143f-5ac7-a0ed-5faf8562286b"] ["question-e6e3c2bf-143f-5ac7-a0ed-5faf8562286b" :question/math-academy-id "q-147965"] ["question-e6e3c2bf-143f-5ac7-a0ed-5faf8562286b" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.11$ | $0.44$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.09$ | $0.36$ |\n\nCalculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$\n\n*Hint: It can be shown that $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible values of $x$ and $y.$*"] ["question-e6e3c2bf-143f-5ac7-a0ed-5faf8562286b" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nWe're told that\n\n$$\nP(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)\n$$\n\nfor all possible values of $x$ and $y.$ Therefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent. \n\nSince $X$ are $Y$ are independent, we have $\\text{Cov}(X,Y)=0.$"] ["question-e6e3c2bf-143f-5ac7-a0ed-5faf8562286b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-a285d13c-8e91-53ff-befc-22c00f6c4f72" :answer-field/id #uuid "a285d13c-8e91-53ff-befc-22c00f6c4f72"] ["answer-9f890194-e25d-57ba-b7d6-5ea090499c5b" :answer/id #uuid "9f890194-e25d-57ba-b7d6-5ea090499c5b"] ["answer-9f890194-e25d-57ba-b7d6-5ea090499c5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9f890194-e25d-57ba-b7d6-5ea090499c5b" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-3a0eed03-c823-52d2-9d91-5f4f57fccf4b" :answer/id #uuid "3a0eed03-c823-52d2-9d91-5f4f57fccf4b"] ["answer-3a0eed03-c823-52d2-9d91-5f4f57fccf4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3a0eed03-c823-52d2-9d91-5f4f57fccf4b" :answer/value "0.01"] ["answer-c6be9011-10e2-579c-9b58-794b4bedb4ae" :answer/id #uuid "c6be9011-10e2-579c-9b58-794b4bedb4ae"] ["answer-c6be9011-10e2-579c-9b58-794b4bedb4ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c6be9011-10e2-579c-9b58-794b4bedb4ae" :answer/value "0.03"] ["answer-007b88eb-e604-58da-b447-a95dc8bd2d6a" :answer/id #uuid "007b88eb-e604-58da-b447-a95dc8bd2d6a"] ["answer-007b88eb-e604-58da-b447-a95dc8bd2d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-007b88eb-e604-58da-b447-a95dc8bd2d6a" :answer/value "0.1"] ["answer-75de5ea3-85e7-5be2-9550-6f79d2d4cd24" :answer/id #uuid "75de5ea3-85e7-5be2-9550-6f79d2d4cd24"] ["answer-75de5ea3-85e7-5be2-95